  "Description": "Removes the fractional part of a value.\n\nThe value is cast to an integer, so it is truncated towards zero: 2.7 becomes 2, but -2.7 becomes -2 (not -3). Values beyond the 32-bit integer range are not handled.\n\nAKA: truncate, int\n\nSee also: [Round], [Ceil]",
